EbolaLens stage 01 source-registry report
=========================================

Investigation (2026-09-06)
--------------------------
All requests were sequential and read-only, with an EbolaLens user agent, a
5-second connection timeout, a 15-second total timeout, redirects enabled, and
bounded response sizes. Temporary responses were stored only under /tmp.

- https://insp.cd/ -> HTTP 200; exposed WordPress REST metadata and links to
  the SitRep category and individual SitRep posts.
- https://insp.cd/wp-json/ -> HTTP 200, application/json.
- https://insp.cd/wp-json/wp/v2/search?search=sitrep&per_page=10 -> HTTP 200;
  returned 10 SitRep post candidates, but search ranking is not a durable index.
- https://insp.cd/category/sitrep/feed/ -> HTTP 200, application/rss+xml;
  contained official post links and embedded PDF metadata. This confirmed RSS
  endpoint is the only automatic discovery mechanism enabled in stage 01.
- https://insp.cd/wp-sitemap.xml -> HTTP 404.
- https://insp.cd/robots.txt -> HTTP 200, general access allowed; it declared
  https://insp.cd/sitemap.xml.
- https://insp.cd/sitemap.xml -> HTTP 404.
- The first sandboxed request could not resolve insp.cd; the same bounded request
  succeeded after explicit network approval. This was a local sandbox limitation,
  not recorded as an INSP service failure.

Implementation
--------------
- Added a validated, maintained JSON registry at data/sources.json with three
  official source pages, the confirmed INSP RSS endpoint, and three confirmed
  INSP seed-document URLs.
- Added only small synthetic offline fixtures; no live PDF bytes were committed.
- Added standard-library retrieval with descriptive user agent, 15-second timeout,
  a 10 MiB bound, redirects, ETag/Last-Modified conditional requests, SHA-256
  payload identity, alias consolidation, retained failures, and atomic manifest
  replacement.
- Added deterministic JSON state and concise text summaries. Runtime state is
  generated at data/generated/source_manifest.json and ignored by Git.
- Added CLI list, offline check, and live check commands while preserving the
  version command.
- Added deterministic network-free tests for configuration validation, RSS
  discovery, unchanged and changed payloads, URL aliases, failure retention,
  atomic writing, offline CLI behavior, and the existing version behavior.
- Updated README.md, data/README.md, and added docs/source_investigation.md.

