Limitations and assumptions
---------------------------
- RSS may omit history or disappear; discovered URLs remain candidates and are
  not automatically treated as registered or epidemiologically valid documents.
- WordPress REST was reachable but is not automatically queried in stage 01.
- Both tested sitemap URLs returned 404. WHO pages are monitored but not scraped.
- Report numbers and dates visible only in filenames remain null until explicitly
  verified from authoritative metadata; filenames are never document identity.
- A successful HTTP response validates reachability and byte identity only, not
  epidemiological contents.
- The stage 00 control artifacts were not modified. No git add, commit, push,
  release, or GitHub operation was performed.
- The unified diff excludes itself to avoid recursive content.

Review correction 01a — manifest isolation and candidate history
=================================================================

Corrections implemented
-----------------------
- Live checks retain data/generated/source_manifest.json as their default state.
  Offline checks now default to data/generated/offline_source_manifest.json.
  CLI parsing leaves --manifest unset until the selected mode is known; an
  explicit path overrides either default.
- Removed the pre-correction data/generated/source_manifest.json after confirming
  it had been created by the earlier synthetic offline verification. It was an
  ignored generated file, not committed state, and can be regenerated only by a
  future live check. The isolated offline manifest remains available.
- Added a cumulative, URL-keyed candidate registry with publisher, discovery
  endpoint, first-seen and last-seen UTC timestamps, current-response presence,
  and per-run newly-discovered classification.
- A later successful feed marks missing candidates not currently present without
  deleting them. Transport and XML failures preserve prior candidate history and
  last successful presence state.
- Summaries now report total, new, and currently present candidate counts, print
  new URLs for human review, and include source/discovery error details.
- Candidate URLs are not fetched or registered automatically and receive no
  inferred identity or epidemiological validation.
- Audited HTTP 304 behavior and added a regression test proving that ETag and
  Last-Modified values remain effective for subsequent conditional checks.
- Fixed a confirmed audit bug: an RSS XML parse failure previously retained an
  endpoint status of "ok" while setting an error. It now reports status "error"
  and preserves the prior successful endpoint and candidate details.

